{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} How To Create Datazone}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} How_To_Create_Datazone}
\pard\keepn \plain\fs36 How To Create a new \uldb Datazone\plain\fs36 {\v J3NDYE@imgmgr.hlp}
\par \pard \fs24 To create a datazone from scratch
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Call the annotation tool bar with \b <CTRL + A>
\par \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Create a Sticky Panel object by clicking on the icon \{bmc bm1.bmp\}  then Click and Drag on the image to create the required size and position of rectangle.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Change the properties of the panel by right clicking on it while selected and selecting the \b Properties\plain\fs22  required 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Create the objects you want on the Datazone, e.g. Parameters by clicking on \{bmc bm2.bmp\} then clicking on the image
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Drag the objects onto the Sticky Panel to the required positions
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Lock the panel by selecting it, right button click on it, select \b Properties\plain\fs22  -\b  Lock this panel
\par \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Convert Panel to be the Current Datazone by selecting it, right button click on it, select \b Properties\plain\fs22  -\b  \fs24 Make Current Datazone
\par 
\par Note 1:\plain\fs24  You may create several Sticky Panels as datazones\b  \plain\fs24 by using the Property \b Make Panel A Datazone,\plain\fs24  these will all be hidden/shown by the macro special function Datazone Off/On, however there is only \b One\plain\fs24  Current Datazone which is automatically loaded and controlled by \fs22  \b <CTRL + D>\plain\fs22  , this is the one that is designated by \b Make \fs24 Current Datazone
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 Note 2: \plain\fs24 You may always revert to the default datazone (which destroys your modified datazone) using the Top Menu Function \b View\plain\fs24  - \b Datazone\plain\fs24  -\b  Display Default Datazone
\par Note 3: \plain\fs24 If you require a selection of different datazones see \uldb \b Save/Load datazones\plain\b\fs24 {\v How_To_save_load_User_Datazones}
\par Note 3: \plain\fs24 Datazone objects will not be saved when saving annotation to file, if you wish to save them to a file you must first select the property \b Don't make Panel a Datazone\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \uldb \b\fs22 Annotating the Image\plain\b\fs22 {\v B7ZV5W@ImgMgr.hlp}
\par 
\par \uldb How to edit the Datazone\plain\b\fs22 {\v How_To_Edit_the_Datazone}\plain\fs24 
