\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Call the annotation tool bar with \b <CTRL + A>
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 If the Datazone is not on display then display it with \b <CTRL + D>
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 Select the Datazone by clicking on it. Blue\ul  handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@ImgMgr.hlp} will be displayed.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Unlock the datazone by clicking on it with the right mouse button and selecting \b Properties\plain\fs22  - \b Unlock this panel
\par \plain\fs24 
\par \fs22 You can now modify the datazone by 
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Changing the position/size of the datazone (drag the datazone or it's handles)
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Dragging objects off the Datazone or to new positions on the datazone
