\pard\keepn\tx355 \plain\fs36 How to Set Up a Common Toolbar
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 Follow these steps to set up a \uldb Common Toolbar\plain\fs24 {\v 5XXH_AL@tooledit.hlp}
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Using the \uldb Toolbar Editor\plain\fs22 {\v Contents@tooledit.hlp} (Top Menu - Edit - Toolbar) create the toolbar with the required functionality.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Save the toolbar file using the\b  SaveAs Common\plain\fs22  button on the first tab of the editor (Note - this button is only available if you have\uldb  Supervisor privilege\plain\fs22 {\v XTAC5O@admin32.hlp}).\fs24 
\par 
\par \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Using the \uldb Administrator\plain\fs22 {\v Contents@admin32.hlp} (Start - Programs - Leo32 - Administrator) set the \b Use Common Toolbar \plain\fs22 attribute for each User required. (Double Click on the Username to access the User Profile)
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx715 \fs22 NOTE: All the Macros required for the Toolbar must be accessible to each User. If necessary provide them as \uldb Common Macros\plain\fs22 {\v HBU_9D@leom.hlp}.
