{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} How to Adjust the Detector Signal}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} How_to_Adjust_the_Detector_Signal}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs28 How to Adjust the Detector Signal\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 The most frequently used functions are control of brightness and contrast of a detector. The setting can be manual or automatic. Additional settings are available.\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Manual Control:\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm6.bmp\} with the left button to switch mouse adjustment to contrast and brightness control \{bmc bm7.bmp\}.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b sensitivity\plain\fs22  of the mouse adjustment by clicking on \{bmc bm8.bmp\} and \{bmc bm9.bmp\} or use 
\par \tab \b <Tab>\plain\fs22  \{bmc bm10.bmp\}.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Adjust \b brightness\plain\fs22  by moving the mouse with the left mouse button pressed.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Adjust \b contrast\plain\fs22  by moving the mouse with the middle mouse button pressed.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \b\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 Collector adjustment of  Secondary electron detector:
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs22 The collector of the  detector can be adjusted to select the ratio of secondary electrons to back scattered electrons to display topography contrast.\b\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Type \b <Ctrl + G>\plain\fs22  The \b SEM Control\plain\fs22  panel opens.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on the\b  Detectors\plain\fs22  tab to bring it forward.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Adjust \b Collector Bias\plain\fs22  from negative to positive bias voltage:
\par \tab Negative: \tab SE suppressed, only BSE.
\par \tab Positive\tab SE collected in addition to BSE.
\par 
\par \b\fs24 Input Look-up Table:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Note: \plain\fs22 Manipulating the\b  Input LUT\plain\fs22  changes linearity of the signal as it is collected into the frame store. In cannot be undone on a saved image.\b\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Type \b <Ctrl + G>\plain\fs22  The \b SEM Control\plain\fs22  panel opens.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on the\b  Detectors\plain\fs22  tab to bring it forward.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \uldb Input LUT Mode\plain\fs22 {\v V4.G6Q@TabMgr.HLP} by clicking on the respective \ul Radio Button\plain\fs22 {\v 2R6X4F@SEM.HLP}.
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Transparent:\plain\fs22  Input LUT has no effect on signal.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Gamma:\plain\fs22  Non linear \ul Gamma\plain\fs22 {\v GAMMA@SEM.HLP} function. Adjust Gamma value with the Gamma \ul Scroll Bar\plain\fs22 {\v 2HOSDE@SEM.HLP}.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Inverse\plain\fs22  for inverted signal (black and white exchanged).
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b User\plain\fs22  to generate your own LUT with the \uldb LUT Editor\plain\fs22 {\v 19GOXJ.@LutMgr.HLP}.\b  
\par \plain\fs22 
