{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs28 How to Annotate the Image\plain\fs36 
\par \pard \fs24 
\par \fs22 Annotation provides a comprehensive means of putting additional information on the SEM image. Text, SEM Parameter Data, and even bitmaps (like logos etc.) can easily be added to the image.
\par \fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Call the annotation tool bar with \b <CTRL + A>\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Text annotation\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 Text annotation can be directly called with \b <CTRL + T>
\par \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Alternatively call text annotation from the annotation tool bar by \ul clicking\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm11.bmp\} and then click on the location in the \uldb Image Window\plain\fs22 {\v GIRNF0@SEM.HLP} where you want to position the text.. An input panel opens. 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Type in the text and quit the panel with \b OK.
\par \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} the text to the required position.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Scale the text using \ul handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@SEM.HLP}.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click in text with the right mouse button to open the \uldb properties menu\plain\fs22 {\v 7BRJ3O@ImgMgr.HLP} to change font, style, colour etc. of text.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Other annotation\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Include any \uldb parameter\plain\fs22 {\v 14QG3AV@ImgMgr.HLP} of the SEM in the annotation overlay by clicking on \{bmc bm2.bmp\} in the annotation tool bar.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab You can insert any \uldb bitmap or metafile\plain\fs22 {\v 19QS57O@ImgMgr.HLP} as an annotation object by clicking on \{bmc bm12.bmp\} in the annotation tool bar. These files are created either elsewhere and imported on disk or within the system (MSPaint in the Accessories group in Program Manager) and are useful to display for example a company logo.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Include graphic elements like \uldb line\plain\fs22 {\v 419OYZ4@ImgMgr.HLP}, \uldb rectangle\plain\fs22 {\v 13W0ZTH@ImgMgr.HLP} and \uldb ellipse\plain\fs22 {\v 24SJ0EV@ImgMgr.HLP} in the annotation overlay by clicking on \{bmc bm13.bmp\} or \{bmc bm14.bmp\} or \{bmc bm15.bmp\} in the annotation toolbar and \ul drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} them to size.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Add a rectangle to the overlay plane onto which annotation objects can be "stuck". The \uldb Sticky Panel\plain\fs22 {\v 4NWQ1Q@ImgMgr.HLP} can be transparent or filled with a pattern. Click on \{bmc bm1.bmp\} to call a panel.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Add data from loaded \uldb TIFF images\plain\fs22 {\v 9UC_0J@ImgMgr.HLP} to the annotation plane by clicking on \{bmc bm16.bmp\}.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Data Zone:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 The \uldb data zone\plain\fs24 {\v J3NDYE@ImgMgr.HLP} is a special group of annotation objects which are used to display current parameters, including if required a micron marker showing the base magnification. \fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Toggle data zone ON or OFF using \b <CTRL\'a0+\'a0D>\plain\fs22 .
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} the data zone to position and size it.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab If the data zone is \uldb unlocked\plain\fs22 {\v 33GKLP@ImgMgr.HLP} you may also drag elements of the data zone to position inside the panel.
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Saving and loading annotation:\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs22 Blocks of annotation may be \uldb saved to disk\plain\fs22 {\v 1DH0V85@ImgMgr.HLP} and \uldb loaded from disk\plain\fs22 {\v 140Z.Q@ImgMgr.HLP} (like logos etc.)\b 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm17.bmp\} to save the marked annotation data under a file name of your choice.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm18.bmp\} and select a file to restore the annotation data stored in it.
\par \pard\tx355 \b Note:\plain\fs22  All annotation objects created on screen can be saved or printed with the image by selecting the Overlay plane ON from the \uldb Export TIFF\plain\fs22 {\v B35SJQ@ImgMgr.HLP} Setup menu.
\par \pard\tx355 
