{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} How to Correct for Astigmatism}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} How_to_Correct_for_Astigmatism}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs28 How to Correct for Astigmatism\plain\fs36 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 High resolution images can only be obtained after correct adjustment of astigmatism. Astigmatism (non-roundness of the beam) is caused by either charging of the specimen and applying an asymmetric field that affects the focus of the beam usually in one direction or by a misaligned aperture. \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \b NOTE\plain\fs22  It is a good idea to \uldb check filament current\plain\fs22 {\v 13HR49B@operation.hlp}, \uldb align the beam\plain\fs22 {\v 1LKD_PL@operation.hlp} and \uldb align the final aperture\plain\fs22 {\v 334XEAC@operation.hlp} correctly before adjusting stigmation. \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \f11\fs20 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f4\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \uldb Reduced Raster\plain\fs22 {\v BFKLC0@SEM.HLP} by \ul clicking\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm19.bmp\}.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Choose a suitable field of view at about 5 kX to 10 kX \uldb magnification\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Select_Magnification} containing preferably round features.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm20.bmp\} to switch mouse adjustment to stigmation control.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Focus to optimum focus with the middle mouse button so that the feature does not "smear" in any direction.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Adjust for best focus using the left mouse button. 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \tab Note: Adjusting X and Y direction separately is easier than both together.
