\pard\keepn \b\fs28 How to Edit the Display Look-up Table\plain\fs36 
\par \pard \fs24 
\par \fs22 The appearance of the image display can be enhanced by using the display \uldb look up table editor\plain\fs22 {\v RKSRH1@LutMgr.HLP}, which can be used to change the grey level or colour of any particular grey level in the image. 
\par Further instructions may be obtained by displaying the \uldb Display LUT\plain\fs22 {\v GD50DR@LutMgr.HLP} window and requesting HELP from the menu , however the following guide will be useful for both live and stored images :
\par 
\par \b\fs24 Switching on the LUT editor:\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \b Edit\plain\fs22  in the \uldb Menu Bar\plain\fs22 {\v 8ZP0K4@SEM.HLP} and select \b Display LUT...\plain\fs22  to call the \uldb Toolbar\plain\fs22 {\v 10WSDWG@LutMgr.HLP} together with the \uldb LUT Editor Window\plain\fs22 {\v OIJ5TA@LutMgr.HLP}.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab If the Toolbar is not visible click in the LUT Editor Window with the right mouse button and select \b Show Toolbar\plain\fs22 
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Load a previously saved look up table:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm21.bmp\} and from the \uldb Open LUT\plain\fs22 {\v F86ZW_@LutMgr.HLP} dialog box choose the required file (extension *.OLT).The new look up table is applied and the LUT window and the tool box can be canceled by clicking on \{bmc bm22.bmp\}.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Save a look up table:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 Click on \{bmc bm23.bmp\} for \uldb Save LUT As\plain\fs22 {\v .8WIUO@LutMgr.HLP}.The default file name will be displayed, eg \b Current.olt
\par \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Delete CURRENT and insert the new file name.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on OK button. The new look up table has been saved for future recall\b 
\par \pard\tx355 Note:\plain\fs22  This look up table is still active and can be removed by selecting \uldb Reset\plain\fs22 {\v JYVFXN@LutMgr.HLP}
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Get Help:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 For additional information on how to set the LUT \ul click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the HELP button in the \uldb LUT Editor Window\plain\fs22 {\v OIJ5TA@LutMgr.HLP} or use \uldb Context Sensitive Help\plain\fs22 {\v 4X_H_GQ@SEM.HLP} with \b <F1>\plain\fs22 .
\par \b\fs24 
