{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Contents}
\b\fs28 How to Exchange the Specimen \plain\fs36 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 Before accessing the specimen chamber, the chamber must first be brought to atmospheric pressure and the stage moved down to avoid interference with the final lens.
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs22 N.B.\plain\fs22  For a more detailed description please consult \uldb \b Changing the Specimen\plain\b\fs22 {\v 3WFJ_A.@operation.hlp}\plain\fs22 .
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 Move the stage to the specimen change position: Use the joystick or alternatively if the Store/recall option is installed and exchange position set up this can be done automatically
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab From the \uldb Menu Bar\plain\fs22 {\v 8ZP0K4@SEM.HLP} select \b Stage\plain\fs22 .
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab From the drop down Menu select \b Store/Recall...
\par \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab From the \uldb Stage Points List\plain\fs22 {\v 1JKVBGQ@dlgmgr.hlp} select
\par \tab \b $Exchange\plain\fs22  (The label for the exchange position)
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \b Goto Selected\plain\fs22 .
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \tab The stage will move to the exchange position.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm24.bmp\} to ventilate the chamber. When the chamber is at atmospheric pressure, the door can be pulled open.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Remove the previous specimen, if there is one, by loosening the small locating screw holding the specimen stub in position. Note, any one of a variety of specimen holders may be in use - however, they are all held in position with a small locating screw. To loosen the screw, use the smaller of the two ball-ended drivers provided.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Insert the new specimen and tighten the locating screw.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Close the chamber door.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm24.bmp\} The pumps should now start. when the vacuum status has reached Ready it is indicated in the status bar by Vac:\{bmc bm25.bmp\}.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Resume specimen examination by clicking on EHT:\{bmc bm26.bmp\} and switch theBeam or EHT on \{bmc bm25.bmp\}.
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Note:\plain\fs22  some stage movement may be required to locate the specimen area requiring examination.
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \uldb \fs22 Stage Store/Recall\plain\fs22 {\v 139NVAW@Stage.HLP}
