{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} How to Investigate a Vacuum Leak}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} How_to_Investigate_a_Vacuum_Leak}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Correct for astigmatism}
\b\fs28 How to Investigate a Vacuum Leak\plain\fs36 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs24 
\par \b\fs22 A few simple rules:\plain\fs24 
\par \fs22 
\par \b 1.\plain\fs22 \tab Before looking for a vacuum leak give the vacuum system time to pump. If you have just changed a specimen in a very humid atmosphere the pump down may take longer. If the specimen is wet it may take several minutes If the stage has been left open for long periods it will take longer to pump.
\par 
\par \b 2.\plain\fs22 \tab Vacuum leaks rarely happen by themselves; they are often caused. If you have just done anything to the chamber then that is the most likely cause of the leak. If the specimen has just been changed, check the stage door 'O' ring.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \b 3.\plain\fs22 \tab The most frequent cause of leaks is dust or fibers on 'O' rings. 'O' rings may be cleaned with a fluff free tissue. 'O' ring grease should never be used. Grease traps fibers and may cause leaks.
\par 
\par \b 4.\plain\fs22 \tab Do not use any metal tools to remove 'O' rings from their grooves. A small scratch in the bottom of a groove causes a big leak.
\par 
\par \b Checking vacuum levels:\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 The control of the vacuum system is automatic and software controlled. Actual state of system and high vacuum are displayed on a tab in the \uldb SEM Control window\plain\fs22 {\v C9V9DR@TabMgr.HLP}: 
\par \pard\tx355 \b 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs22 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Type \b <Ctrl + G>\plain\fs22  to display the SEM Control panel, select \uldb Vacuum Tab\plain\fs22 {\v C9V9DR@tabmgr.hlp}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Check the vacuum levels and the status of the vacuum system
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \uldb SEM Control Vacuum\plain\fs22 {\v C9V9DR@TabMgr.HLPairlock@DlgMgr.HLP}
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \uldb Getting a Vacuum\plain\fs22 {\v CVEOUF@operation.hlp}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} How to Make Measurements from the Image}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} How_to_Make_Measurements_from_the_Image}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs28 How to Make Measurements from the Image\plain\fs36 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 There is a wide range of measuring image features.\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Call the annotation tool bar with \b <CTRL\'a0+\'a0A>
\par \plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Magnification and micron markers:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 Zone Magnification and Micron will display the correct magnification and micron marker bar for the zone of the image in which they are positioned, even if the zone has been frozen.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm27.bmp\} to switch the \uldb Zone Magnification\plain\fs22 {\v 3MD42KU@ImgMgr.HLP} function ON and click to the zone for which you want to show magnification.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm28.bmp\} to switch the variable \uldb Micron Marker\plain\fs22 {\v 6A8V0Z@ImgMgr.HLP} function ON and click to the zone for which you want to show the marker.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm29.bmp\} to switch the \uldb Fixed Micron Bar\plain\fs22 {\v 36ZDQY@ImgMgr.HLP} function ON and click to the zone for which you want to show the marker.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Width and height measurements:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Line Width\plain\fs22  displays a box which can be positioned over a feature, such as a semiconductor line, and the width and breadth of the box displayed.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm30.bmp\} to switch \uldb Line Width\plain\fs22 {\v 696WT5@ImgMgr.HLP} mode ON.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Point to the zone in which you want to place the Line Width rectangle and click.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on the box and \ul drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} the \ul handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@SEM.HLP} as required.
\par \pard\tx355 \b Width Measurement\plain\fs22  can be made between a related pair of vertical lines:
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm31.bmp\} to switch \uldb Width Measurement\plain\fs22 {\v NQ.CYT@ImgMgr.HLP} ON.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Point to the zone in which you want to place the measuring lines and click.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on the lines, pick the \ul handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@SEM.HLP} and \ul drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} them.
\par \pard\tx355 \b Adjustable Width Measurement\plain\fs22  is similar but also allows to adjust the lines vertically too.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm32.bmp\} to switch \uldb Adjustable Width Measurement\plain\fs22 {\v G4QYQ5@ImgMgr.HLP} ON.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Point to the zone in which you want to place the measuring lines and click.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on the lines, pick the \ul handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@SEM.HLP} and \ul drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} them.
\par \pard\tx355 \b Height Measurement\plain\fs22  can be made between a related pair of vertical lines:
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm33.bmp\} to switch \uldb Height Measurement\plain\fs22 {\v 1KIQST5@ImgMgr.HLP} ON.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Point to the zone in which you want to place the measuring lines and click.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on the lines, pick the \ul handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@SEM.HLP} and \ul drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} them.
\par \pard\tx355 \b Adjustable Height Measurement\plain\fs22  is similar but also allows to adjust the lines horizontally too.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm34.bmp\} to switch \uldb Adjustable Height Measurement\plain\fs22 {\v 25MKEKI@ImgMgr.HLP} ON.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Point to the zone in which you want to place the measuring lines and click.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on the lines, pick the \ul handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@SEM.HLP} and \ul drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} them.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Other dimensional measurements:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Point to Point\plain\fs22  displays a pair of pointers which can be positioned against features of the image and the distance displayed. The rotational difference will also be displayed.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm35.bmp\} to switch \uldb Point to Point\plain\fs22 {\v 5QGH.F@ImgMgr.HLP} ON.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Point to the zone in which you want to place the Point to Point marker and click.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on the line, pick the \ul handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@SEM.HLP} and \ul drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} them.
\par \pard\tx355 The \b Angular Measurement\plain\fs22  facility comprises a related pair of measurement lines which may be adjusted in length, angle and position.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm36.bmp\} to switch \uldb Angular Measurement\plain\fs22 {\v .J1WF7@ImgMgr.HLP} ON.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Point to the zone in which you want to place the Angular Measurement markers and click.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on the lines, pick the \ul handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@SEM.HLP} and \ul drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} them.
\par \pard\tx355 The \b Radial Measurement\plain\fs22  facility is a circle which may be adjusted in diameter.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm37.bmp\} to switch \uldb Radial Measurement\plain\fs22 {\v 3BI2_Y0@ImgMgr.HLP}  ON.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Point to the zone in which you want to place the Radial Measurement circle and click.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on the circle, pick the \ul handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@SEM.HLP} and \ul drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} them.
\par \pard\tx355 The \b Stored Vector Profile\plain\fs22  function brings up the profile display along a measurement line on the stored image.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm38.bmp\} to switch \uldb Stored Vector Profile\plain\fs22 {\v 1NSP15O@ImgMgr.HLP} ON.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Draw a line and \ul drag\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} the line with the \ul handles\plain\fs22 {\v K6O1DR@SEM.HLP} into position. The grey level profile along the line will be shown.
\par \pard\tx355 The \b Stored Data Histogram\plain\fs22  function displays a histogram of the stored image.\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm39.bmp\} to switch the\uldb  Stored Data Histogram\plain\fs22 {\v HYW4LM@ImgMgr.HLP} function ON.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Draw a rectangle around the area in the image for which you want to show the histogram.
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Note:\plain\fs22  All measurement objects created on screen can be saved or printed with the image by selecting the Overlay plane ON from the \uldb Export TIFF\plain\fs22 {\v B35SJQ@ImgMgr.HLP} Setup menu.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \uldb Zone Magnification\plain\fs22 {\v 3MD42KU@ImgMgr.HLP}
\par \tab \uldb Micron Marker\plain\fs22 {\v 6A8V0Z@ImgMgr.HLP}
