{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} How to Noise Reduce and Freeze the Image}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} How_to_Noise_Reduce_and_Freeze_the_Image}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs28 How to Noise Reduce and Freeze the Image\plain\fs36 
\par \pard \fs24 
\par \fs22 Comprehensive noise reduction facilities are provided on the instrument, and these are very valuable both as an aid to image optimisation in low signal conditions and as a way of reviewing the image prior to saving or hard-copy.
\par Three methods of noise reduction are used: Frame Integration,Frame Averaging and Line Averaging.
\par \fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Frame Integration is useful when applied to beam sensitive materials, since the image can be obtained while the beam remains scanning quickly and not allowed to dwell too long on any point of the specimen. In this mode the image formed as the average of a \ul number of successive frames\plain\fs22 {\v EQNXF7@TabMgr.HLP} .
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab In Frame Averaging mode\fs24  \fs22 frames are scanned continuously and the image formed as the average of a \ul number of successive frames\plain\fs22 {\v 117K7K3@tabmgr.hlpContinuous_Average_Mode@TabMgr.HLPPixel_Average_mode@TabMgr.HLP}
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Line Averaging is useful\fs24  when the result of the noise reduction needs to be seen without waiting for the cycle to complete. The image is built up by \ul averaging a number of lines\plain\fs24 {\v PHG8LG@tabmgr.hlp}\fs22 
\par 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Use \{bmc bm40.bmp\} for Frame averaging - (\uldb Icon Definition\plain\fs22 {\v ZYLMCP@sem.hlp})
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Use \{bmc bm41.bmp\} for Frame Integration (\uldb Icon Definition\plain\fs22 {\v ZYLMFM@sem.hlp})
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Use \{bmc bm42.bmp\} for Line averaging (\uldb Icon Definition\plain\fs22 {\v ZYLMFR@sem.hlp})
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Selecting the Scan Speed
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 Click on \{bmc bm43.bmp\} to scan slower
\par \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 Click on \{bmc bm44.bmp\} to scan faster
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on menu \b Scanning - Scan rate\plain\fs24  to select a specific scan rate\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b\fs24 
\par \plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Freezing\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 To capture an image for storage or printing, the image store must first be \uldb frozen\plain\fs22 {\v 2G1LTFP@SEM.HLP}. Two methods of freezing are provided which are set in the \uldb SEM Control Scanning\plain\fs22 {\v R5KU.@TabMgr.HLP} panel under 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Freeze on =\plain\fs22  
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \tab \b END FRAME\plain\fs22  freezes the image at the end of the frame and effectively converts the noise reduction from averaging to integration.
\par \pard\tx715 
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \tab \b COMMAND\plain\fs22  freezes the image when you click on \{bmc bm45.bmp\} instantly.
\par \pard\tx715 A frozen zone is marked with a blue dot \{bmc bm46.bmp\} in the lower right corner.
\par \pard\tx715 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab To resume live imaging, click on the pause icon \{bmc bm45.bmp\} again. The selected mode of noise reduction will resume.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Note: \plain\fs22 When used with split or quad screen mode, the above freezing method will selectively freeze the half of the image containing the \{bmc bm47.bmp\} icon. The icon can be \ul dragged\plain\fs22 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} to the zone which shall be frozen.
\par \pard\tx355 If the icon is \{bmc bm48.bmp\} both halves will be frozen. Double-clicking the anchor icon will change between the two states, i.e. single zone and both zones.
\par \pard\tx355 
