{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} How to Optimise the Image}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} How_to_Optimise_the_Image}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs28 How to Optimise the Image\plain\fs36 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par 
\par \fs22 
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Is the \uldb Filament saturated and Gun Aligned\plain\fs22 {\v S5.G0D@operation.hlp}? If not, a loss of signal and resolution will be seen.
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Is the \uldb aperture aligned\plain\fs22 {\v 334XEAC@operation.hlp}?. Misalignment prevents good resolution and causes astigmatism
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Is the \uldb stigmation adjusted\plain\fs22 {\v 7TVA0H0@sem.hlp} correctly? Incorrect adjustment will show in the image as a directional "smearing" of focus.
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Is the \uldb correct detector\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Select_the_Detector} selected?\uldb  Information content\plain\fs22 {\v 3LPLSPE@sem.hlp} of the image is strongly influenced by the type of detector in use.
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Is the \uldb signal of the detector\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Adjust_the_Detector_Signal} adjusted? Contrast and Brightness play an important part in image appearance. Too much contrast may enhance noise content, not enough contrast makes the image "flat".
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab Is the \uldb collector adjustment\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Adjust_the_Detector_Signal} of the secondary detector correct? Incorrect adjustment may result in loss of signal.
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab is the correct \uldb scan speed\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Noise_Reduce_and_Freeze_the_Image} selected? Lower scan speed reduces noise and enhances representation of small detail.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par If none of the above see \uldb \b Advanced Operation\plain\b\fs22 {\v 18GQS0@operation.hlp}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} How to Restore/Save the System Conditions}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} How_to_Restore_Save_the_System_Conditions}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \fs28 How to Restore/Save the System Conditions\plain\fs36 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\} \tab \plain\ul\fs22 Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm49.bmp\} to \b restore\plain\fs22  the system to the conditions as they were when the system was shut down (user specific).\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab You may wish to \b install conditions\plain\fs22  from a previously stored file\b .\plain\fs22  From the \b File\plain\fs22  menu, select \b Load State\plain\fs22  - you will then see a list of saved state files in your directory (*.MLC). If the required file is in another directory or on a floppy disk, you will need to select the directory as appropriate from the menu. Having highlighted the file, press OK - the conditions will now be installed. 
\par \tab Remember, if any part of the system configuration has changed since the file was saved, you will be asked whether to proceed with the run up or not. It is also a good idea to check the \uldb gun alignment.\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Align_the_Electron_Beam}
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \b Save the system conditions for restore without closing interface\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 In the\b  \uldb Menu Bar\plain\b\fs22 {\v 8ZP0K4@SEM.HLP} \plain\fs22 click on\b  \uldb File\plain\b\fs22 {\v 6XNXVL@SEM.HLP}.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 Click on\b  Save for Restore
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \b Save the system conditions\plain\fs22  when you \uldb Log Off\plain\fs22 {\v 7N1CWQ@SEM.HLP} or \uldb Exit\plain\fs22 {\v YDV_M4@SEM.HLP}:
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab In the \uldb Menu Bar\plain\fs22 {\v 8ZP0K4@SEM.HLP} click on \uldb File\plain\fs22 {\v 6XNXVL@SEM.HLP}.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \b Log OFF\plain\fs22  or
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \b Exit
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 Click on \b YES\plain\fs22  when you are asked if you want to save the SEM conditions.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \uldb Store / Restore System Conditions\plain\fs22 {\v 2U782Q@SEM.HLP}
\par \tab \uldb Standard Conditions\plain\fs22 {\v Z1JVVC@LEOM.HLP}
