{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} How to Run up the Electron Beam}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} How_to_Run_up_the_Electron_Beam}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs28 How to Run up the Electron Beam\plain\fs36 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs22 Note: \plain\fs22 Only when the operating vacuum is obtained can the high voltage be activated. The high voltage is switched off automatically when the chamber is ventilated (safety interlock). The high voltage is also switched off with poor vacuum in the gun.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 There are three main ways to run up the electron beam automatically. Additionally, the beam may be run up manually :\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b\fs22 1.\plain\fs22 \tab The easiest and most convenient method is simply to \ul click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} \{bmc bm49.bmp\} with the left mouse button. This runs up the beam to exactly the last conditions used in your directory (from the macro file RESTORE0.MLC). \b 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b 2.\plain\f11\fs22 \tab \f4 You may wish to install conditions from a previously \b stored file.\plain\fs22  From \uldb Menu File\plain\fs22 {\v 6XNXVL@SEM.HLP} menu, select \uldb Load State\plain\fs22 {\v 2ICG_3B@SEM.HLP} - you will then see a list of saved state files in your directory. If the required file is in another directory or on a floppy disk, you will need to select the directory as appropriate from the menu. Having highlighted the file, press OK - the conditions will now be installed. It is also a good idea to check the \uldb electron beam alignment\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Align_the_Electron_Beam}\b . \plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs20 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b\fs22 3.\plain\fs22 \tab If you are unsure what conditions to use, a useful facility is provided in \uldb Menu File\plain\fs22 {\v 6XNXVL@SEM.HLP}, called \uldb Standard\plain\fs22 {\v I3EDZI@SEM.HLP}. Selection of Standard executes a default run up from which the conditions may be further adjusted. 
\par \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 If any part of the system configuration has changed since the file was saved, you will be asked whether to proceed with the run up or not.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b Manually: \plain\fs22 On the \uldb Status Bar\plain\fs22 {\v RDJHU5@SEM.HLP} click on \b EHT\plain\fs22  and select \b Beam On \{bmc bm50.bmp\}\plain\fs22   The gun will be run up to \{bmc bm25.bmp\}. To adjust parameters you may use \uldb Menu Tools\plain\fs22 {\v 6V_3A4@SEM.HLP}, \uldb Goto Control Panel\plain\fs22 {\v 1XGV9QP@SEM.HLP}, \uldb SEM Control Gun\plain\fs22 {\v 5_0HOO@TabMgr.HLP}. 
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \uldb Switching the Electron Beam\plain\fs22 {\v 124_W53@sem.hlp}
\par 
\par \tab \uldb Menu Beam\plain\fs22 {\v 6XJTKT@SEM.HLP}
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 
