\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Create Datazone;Edit the display look up table;Exchange the specimen}
\b\fs28 How to Select Magnification\plain\fs36 
\par \pard \fs24 
\par \fs22 Magnification can be adjusted with the mouse, selected from the magnification table, selected from a predefined list, or typed in with the keyboard:\fs24 
\par 
\par \b Mouse selection\plain\fs24 :
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \{bmc bm4.bmp\} with the left mouse button
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Adjust magnification moving the mouse and holding down the left mouse button.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Sensitivity of mouse action can be selected in the \uldb Status Bar\plain\fs22 {\v RDJHU5@SEM.HLP} clicking on \{bmc bm8.bmp\} and \{bmc bm9.bmp\} or using \b <Tab>\plain\fs22  \{bmc bm51.bmp\}.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Magnification is displayed in the Status Bar when the mouse is in Mag/Focus mode.
\par \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Magnification table:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab With function key \b <F4> \plain\fs22 you may toggle through the set of magnifications as set in Preference Selection / \uldb Magnification Table.\plain\fs22 {\v 1_WKN3Z@LEOServ.HLP}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Function keys \b <Shift + F4>\plain\fs22  reset to the original magnification before you pressed \b <F4>\plain\fs22  the first time.
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Predefined list:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\plain\fs22 \tab Click on \{bmc bm52.bmp\} MAG-field with the right mouse button. The list of predefined magnifications opens.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on a value to select it.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \b Close\plain\fs22  button to close the list.
\par \b\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 Keyboard input:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b\fs24 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\plain\fs22 \tab Click on \{bmc bm52.bmp\} MAG-field with the left mouse button. The parameter input panel opens.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Enter the magnification value.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Close the panel clicking on \b OK\plain\fs22  button.
\par \b\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab 
\par \tab \uldb Magnification Table\plain\fs22 {\v FWN3HJ@SEM.HLP}
\par \tab \uldb Magnification Table Setup\plain\fs22 {\v 1_WKN3Z@LEOServ.HLP}
