{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} How To Edit the datazone}
\b\fs28 How to Select the Detector\plain\fs36 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 Which detector to use depends on the imaging characteristics of the individual detector.\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Changing the detector channel:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the \b Detection / Detectors\plain\fs22  menu and \ul click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the title of the desired detector from the list displayed.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Adjust \uldb contrast and brightness\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Adjust_the_Detector_Signal} as necessary in the normal way
\par \tab \b Note:\plain\fs22  Contrast and brightness settings for each detector will be recalled on switching
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Split screen image in different signals:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 Click on \{bmc bm53.bmp\} to switch to split mode.
\par \tab \b Note:\plain\fs22  Any previous detector and/or LUT selections for each half will be recalled
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Drag the \{bmc bm47.bmp\} icon to the half intended to display the new signal.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the \b Detection / Detectors\plain\fs22  menu and \ul click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the title of the desired detector from the list displayed.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Repeat for other half as required\b 
\par \pard\tx355 Note:\plain\fs22  Freeze and Contrast and Brightness can be adjusted specifically for the half containing the anchor. Gamma, Invert, and Mixing, apply to both zones in common.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Signal Mixing\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \cf1 Mixing is used to mix the proportions of signals from two detectors.
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Type \b <Ctrl + G>\plain\fs22\cf1   to display the SEM Control Panel\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the \uldb \b Detectors\plain\b\fs22 {\v 1WE3854@tabmgr.hlp}\plain\fs22  tab to bring it forward. Proceed as above except now \b Signal B\plain\fs22  can be assigned to any of the installed detectors.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Mixing\plain\fs22  \{bmc bm54.bmp\}.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Use the \b Signal\plain\fs22  \ul scroll bar\plain\fs22 {\v 2HOSDE@SEM.HLP} to vary the ratio of Signal (A) to Signal (B).
\par \tab \b Note:\plain\fs22  Having set this up, it can all be saved through the \uldb Save State\plain\fs22 {\v I6NCK5@SEM.HLP} function.
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab 
