\pard\keepn\tx355 {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} How to Investigate a Vacuum Leak}
\b\fs28 How to Store or Load an Image\plain\fs36 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 After finding an area of interest on the specimen, fully \uldb optimising the image\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Optimise_the_Image} and \uldb freezing\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Noise_Reduce_and_Freeze_the_Image} it, it may then be stored to disk for future use. 
\par \pard\tx355 Stored images can be loaded back into the image store for further processing.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Save the image:\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click with the Right button on the image and select  \uldb \b Export TIFF\plain\b\fs22 {\v B35SJQ@ImgMgr.HLP} \plain\fs22 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click \plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP}on the \uldb Save\plain\fs22 {\v 8BP7F1@ImgMgr.HLP} tab to bring it forward.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the parameters for saving:
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the \ul area\plain\fs22 {\v UKJGL_@ImgMgr.HLP} to save
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select what to \ul merge\plain\fs22 {\v FFGUZT@ImgMgr.HLP} into the image
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Input file name (see also \uldb settings\plain\fs22 {\v 1M2_ZSF@ImgMgr.HLP})
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Input \ul user text\plain\fs22 {\v 8CBB8D@ImgMgr.HLP}
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the \uldb Settings\plain\fs22 {\v 1M2_ZSF@ImgMgr.HLP} tab to bring it forward.
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select grey or colour \ul radio button\plain\fs22 {\v 2R6X4F@SEM.HLP}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b As Seen\plain\fs22  if the image pixels are to be transformed by the Look Up Table before exporting
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Palette\plain\fs22  if the palette is to be saved in the file (recommended)
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the amount of spatial reduction to be performed on the exported image
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the \ul Filename Format\plain\fs22 {\v F7ZT7A@ImgMgr.HLP}
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the \uldb Data\plain\fs22 {\v 8BA7CX@ImgMgr.HLP} tab to bring it forward. This tab allows you to select parameter data to be saved in Leo Reserved Tag fields embedded in the TIFF file.
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} \b ADD\plain\fs22  to select a parameter to be added to the list
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select a parameter in the list and click \b REMOVE\plain\fs22  to remove it from the list
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click \plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP}on the \uldb Save\plain\fs22 {\v 8BP7F1@ImgMgr.HLP} tab to bring it forward again
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Save the file by pressing the \b SAVE\plain\fs22  button
\par 
\par \b\fs24 Load an image:
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 Call the \uldb Import TIFF\plain\fs22 {\v 1JWFSX0@ImgMgr.HLP} menu with \b <CTRL\'a0+\'a0O>
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\plain\fs22 \tab Select the \uldb Load\plain\fs22 {\v 6LG1R4@ImgMgr.HLP} tab to bring it forward. The list box displays the current files in the image directory.
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 Click on GALLERY button in the Load tab to display the \uldb Image Gallery\plain\fs22 {\v Contents@Gallery.HLP} for a quick pictorial overview.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select a file in the list box of the Load tab to display it's information and \ul user text\plain\fs22 {\v 8CBB8D@ImgMgr.HLP}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the amount of spatial reduction required
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \ul where to load\plain\fs22 {\v CTB1BD@ImgMgr.HLP} the image\b 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \uldb Standard Data\plain\fs22 {\v _ZA_P9@ImgMgr.HLP} tab to inspect the data which were stored with the image
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \uldb User Data\plain\fs22 {\v 19Z7CGA@ImgMgr.HLP} tab to inspect the data which were selected by the user to be stored with the image
\par 
\par \b\fs24 Selecting the directory:
\par \plain\fs24 This is done via the \b Change Directory \plain\fs24  button on the Load/Save Tab\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 This function permits the \uldb Image Directory\plain\fs22 {\v 11JZ0YM@LEOServ.HLP} to be selected or changed.
\par \pard\tx355 
