{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} How to Take a Micrograph or print}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} How_to_Take_a_Micrograph_or_print}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} How To save/load User Datazones}
\b\fs28 How to Take a Micrograph or print\plain\fs36 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs22 Whether you can take a micrograph or print will depend on the configuration of the microscope, i.e. whether a  printer or the High Resolution Recording Unit (HRRU), or both, have been installed.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Preparation:\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \uldb \plain\uldb\fs22 Optimise the image\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Optimise_the_Image} area to be printed, including \uldb focus\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Adjust_Focus} and \uldb stigmation\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Correct_for_Astigmatism}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Optimise \uldb contrast and brightness\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Adjust_the_Detector_Signal}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Apply \uldb noise reduction\plain\fs22 {\v How_to_Noise_Reduce_and_Freeze_the_Image}, as necessary, then freeze the image\b 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs24 Print on the default Windows Printer:
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs22  If necessary
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab From the Task Bar select \b Start\plain\fs22  - \b Settings\plain\fs22  - \b Printers\plain\fs22  
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Double click on the required printer icon
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab From the Printer Window menu select \b Printer\plain\fs22  - \b Set As Default (\plain\fs22 if this is not already selected)
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab On the image click the right mouse button and select \b Send To - Printer\plain\fs22 
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select which \ul settings\plain\fs22 {\v FFGUZT@ImgMgr.HLP} should be merged and printed.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select size and position of the print on the page
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on Print button to start the printout
\par 
\par \pard\tx715 \b Print On CP750 Printer:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 Click on \{bmc bm56.bmp\} to clear the screen ready for printing
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Initiate the print on the CP750
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Type \b <Shift + F3>\plain\fs22  to restore User Interface\b 
\par \pard\tx715 \plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx715 \b\fs24 Photographic print:\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs22 With the right mouse button \ul click\plain\fs22 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} in the \uldb Image Window\plain\fs22 {\v GIRNF0@SEM.HLP}
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Send to\plain\fs22  and \ul HRRU\plain\fs22 {\v HRRU@SEM.HLP}, the Photo panel opens.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab If you have used the HRRU in this session before and you want to use the same settings click on the \uldb Photo\plain\fs22 {\v XYH.74@ImgMgr.HLP} button to start the exposure.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab If you have not used the HRRU in this session or if you want to change parameters then set it up:\b 
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \plain\fs22 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \uldb Settings\plain\fs22 {\v 12O7D55@ImgMgr.HLP} tab to bring the panel forward.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the parameters from the \ul drop-down lists\plain\fs22 {\v XYVXW3@SEM.HLP} (film speed, camera type, \ul Gamma\plain\fs22 {\v GAMMA@SEM.HLP}, exposure time and mode)
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \uldb Selection\plain\fs22 {\v 16QR3DO@ImgMgr.HLP} tab to bring the panel forward.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select camera image source from the \ul drop-down list\plain\fs22 {\v XYVXW3@SEM.HLP}, overlay, annotation and set brightness and contrast of the exposure with the \ul scroll bars\plain\fs22 {\v 2HOSDE@SEM.HLP}.
\par \pard\li715\fi-355\tx715 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \uldb Photo\plain\fs22 {\v XYH.74@ImgMgr.HLP} tab to bring it forward.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on Photo button to start the exposure. \cf1 The progress bar indicates how far an individual exposure has progressed. \plain\fs22 Completion of the photo is indicated by Camera status = Idle.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Develop the print and make any further adjustments as necessary.
\par \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \cf1 If you use direct developing film the \uldb Photo Development Timer\plain\fs22\cf1 {\v HWQ376@ImgMgr.HLP}.helps for proper timing.\plain\fs22 
\par \pard\tx355 
